# KNOWN GAP (ASan lane). The value-lane twin is
# tests/fixtures/known_gaps/comprehension_invariant_owned_body_double_free.gg — same program, different lane.
# at runtime (rc 134, `free(): double free detected in tcache 2`).
#
# The comprehension body `s` does not mention the loop variable, so it is
# evaluated to the SAME String three times and THREE ALIASES of one heap buffer
# land in the vector. `s` is still live afterwards, so the compiler contract says
# CLONE — AGENTS.md § "Ownership at Consuming Positions": *"Borrow, OR owned but
# live past this call → clone before call"*, and a comprehension's accumulate is
# a consuming position exactly like `push`. Freeing the array then frees one
# buffer three times:
#
#   ERROR: AddressSanitizer: attempting double-free
#       #1 __gorget_global_dealloc_fn  #2 gorget_string_free
#       #3 gorget_array_free           #4 main
#
# ⚠ THE PAYLOAD MUST BE HEAP-FORCED (`mk("a","b")`, not a literal) or the double
# free is invisible.
#
# ⚠ THE AXIS IS NARROWER THAN "LOOP-INVARIANT BODY". `known_gaps/
# map_inline_closure_cross_type_input_mint.gg` asserts that
# `[mk("t","ag") for n in nums]` — also loop-invariant, also a heap String — is
# CORRECT. The difference is that this body is an already-owned live NAME rather
# than a fresh call result, so the value is aliased instead of minted per
# iteration.
#
# ⚠ NOT todo/t0003. That family's axis is the ACCUMULATOR'S ELEMENT TYPE — the
# result element minted from the source element's size/destructor — and one of
# its recorded symptoms crashes in these very frames (`gorget_string_free` ←
# `gorget_array_free`) by DESTRUCTOR INHERITANCE. Here nothing is mis-minted: the
# element type is right and the values are right, and the program would print the
# correct answer if it did not free three times. Same frames, different cause.
#
# INTENDED (asserted by the wired test): prints ababab.
# Filed as todo/t0841. Found 2026-08-30 by R47 Track F4a.

String mk(String a, String b):
    return a + b


void main():
    String s = mk("a", "b")
    Vector[String] parts = [s for i in 0..3]
    print("".join(parts))
